d "848b178b-00cd-5964-8724-b50b402d0b68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481423 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186481285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481423 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160906" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481423 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481423 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+2y)\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the quadrilateral region with vertices $(1,-\\frac{1}{2}),$ $(\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{3}{4}),$ $(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\pi -3}{4}),$ and $(1,\\frac{\\pi -2}{4}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481423 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3e35845-58c1-5603-a038-b92edbbc2e02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481423 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe integrand\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+2y)\n$$\n\nsuggests that we use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=2x,\\,v=x+2y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nThe vertices of our domain $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(1,-\\frac{1}{2}) & =(2\\cdot 1,1+2(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =(2,0) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{3}{4}) & =(2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2},\\frac{3}{2}+2(-\\frac{3}{4})) \\\\  & =(3,0) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\pi -3}{4}) & =(2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2},\\frac{3}{2}+2(\\frac{\\pi -3}{4})) \\\\  & =(3,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(1,\\frac{\\pi -2}{4}) & =(2\\cdot 1,1+2(\\frac{\\pi -2}{4})) \\\\  & =(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/dd/dd628fd99b4684d79e8c3b0f4e6696f72582abaef18eef729f5611711a2e42ec.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+2y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,|\\frac{1}{4}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{3}u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,\\text{d}v{\\int }_{2}^{3}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot [\\operatorname{sin}⁡v]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{2}^{3}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 1\\cdot \\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493410 #edb/ref 1080 "3({e}^{-1/2}-{e}^{-2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493410 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493410 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b6b5fe5-29d1-5793-a274-fa3b5699e913" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493432 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{e}{8}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493432 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493432 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17dcff5e-6574-5e2e-be4c-22c67c1a31d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493554 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2}}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493554 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493554 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "702b0bc2-ac10-5437-9f18-9fa877532a9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493601 #edb/ref 1080 "8{e}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493601 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493601 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "857734df-e10d-5568-a049-4e87b8b5c0d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493747 #edb/ref 1080 "({e}^{2}-e)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493747 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493747 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e162164d-9035-55fa-9f1c-b47ea0bae241" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493808 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186493410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493